I just put together a batch file to automate nethack role selection
(Windows specific).  Rather than choose only one role, it rotates
through any role you haven't specifically told it not to play.

Meta-code:
1. Look for PPP.prv file in current directory,
    where PPP=arc,bar,cav,...rog,ran,...,wiz
    in that order
2. If no PPP.prv, act as if wiz.prv exists
3. Delete any existing PPP.prv
4. Advance to next PPP in order given by NH3.4.3
    menu (largely alphabetical, except for rog
    before ran)
5. Look for PPP.win file for new PPP
6. If found, goto step 4
7. Create PPP.prv for new PPP
8. Launch "nethack.exe -p PPP"
9. Exit upon program termination

I figured it would help me be more varied in the classes I play, as
well as trying to discourage me from ascending Valks too much (my only
ascension thus far.  Last week, in fact!)

Call me lazy, but I thought it was a good idea.  It is, however, broken
in a few ways:
a. Must create PPP.win files manually, to imply
    ascension.  The perk of this, however, is
    that you can disallow classes that you
    _haven't_ ascended but just don't want to
    play.
b. Predictable order.  Not a serious flaw, but
    could be more exciting.
c. Breaks if .win files exist for all classes.
    Infinite loop behavior.  This has huge
    numbers of easy fixes, but it's still a flaw
    to be aware of.
d. The code rivals Medusa in beauty.

If anybody is interested in it, and/or has suggestions to make it
better or more useful, it is documented at
http://www.mattborn.net/nethack/rolebat.php


